# Summary

The statute's retention rule states that records of the society are retained for the period named in the schedule of this statute [[cite:obs-313eb37a7e3229dd7cc9bbd1732b8760e0975d8f "Records of the society are retained for the period named in the schedule of this statute."]]. The records are kept for eleven calendar years before shredding [[cite:obs-00f5fb5995a469fa33bba27672e899fd8ff4a2a7 "Ledgers: eleven calendar years, shredding afterwards."]].